# Datepicker Component

## Purpose & Scope

`Datepicker` is a compound component for date selection in the eToro design system. It provides a flexible, accessible date input with:

- **Two display variants**: `inputField` (form-style with floating label) and `compactField` (dropdown-style button)
- **Compound component pattern**: `Datepicker.Label`, `Datepicker.Field`, `Datepicker.CalendarIcon`, `Datepicker.CompactFieldDisplay` subcomponents
- **Native picker integration**: Uses `@react-native-community/datetimepicker` for platform-native date selection
- **Controlled and uncontrolled modes**: Supports both `value` (controlled) and `defaultValue` (uncontrolled)
- **Built-in states**: focus, error, disabled, readonly
- **inputField chrome**: boxed InputV2-like surface (fixed height, radius, fill, full border) — not underline
- **Floating label animation**: Animated label that floats when focused or filled (inputField variant)
- **Context-based state sharing**: No prop drilling, all state shared via React Context
- **Configurable formatting**: Custom date formats using date-fns
- **Locale support**: Internationalization via date-fns locales
- **Value type conversion**: Return Date object, ISO string, or formatted string

**Does NOT handle:**

- Form validation logic (handle in parent)
- Form submission logic (handle in parent)
- Navigation logic (use with router/navigation handlers)
- Custom calendar UI (uses native platform pickers)

## Entry Points & Contracts

### `Datepicker` (main component - context provider)

```tsx
<Datepicker
  variant?: DatepickerVariant            // 'inputField' | 'compactField' (default: 'inputField')
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>           // Container style override
  defaultValue?: Date | string | null   // Initial value for uncontrolled mode
  value?: Date | string | null           // Value for controlled mode
  onChange?: (date: Date | string | null) => void
  mode?: DatepickerMode                  // 'date' (only 'date' is currently supported)
  format?: string                        // date-fns format string (default: 'dd MMM yyyy')
  locale?: Locale                        // date-fns locale
  valueType?: DatepickerValueType        // 'date' | 'iso' | 'formatted' (default: 'date')
  minDate?: Date                         // Minimum selectable date
  maxDate?: Date                         // Maximum selectable date
  error?: string | null                  // Error state (affects label/border styling, auto-renders helper text)
  disabled?: boolean                     // Disabled state (default: false)
  readonly?: boolean                     // Read-only state (default: false)
>
  {children}
</Datepicker>
```

**Children constraints (inputField variant):**

- Must contain `Datepicker.Label` and `Datepicker.Field` at minimum
- Optional: `Datepicker.CalendarIcon` (automatically rendered if not provided)
- Helper text is automatically rendered when `error` exists - do not include it in JSX
- Order matters for visual layout

**Children constraints (compactField variant):**

- Optional: `Datepicker.CompactFieldDisplay` for customization (automatically rendered if not provided)
- Does NOT use `Datepicker.Label`, `Datepicker.Field`, or `Datepicker.CalendarIcon`
- Helper text is automatically rendered when `error` exists

### `Datepicker.Label`

```tsx
<Datepicker.Label
  required?: boolean            // Shows asterisk if required
>
  {string}                      // Label text (e.g., "Date" or "Date (Read only)")
</Datepicker.Label>
```

### `Datepicker.Field`

```tsx
<Datepicker.Field
  placeholder?: string
  ref?: Ref<TextInput>
  testID?: string
  accessibilityLabel?: string
  accessibilityHint?: string
/>
```

**Note:** The field is always readonly - it displays the formatted date and opens the picker on press. All date-related props (`value`, `defaultValue`, `format`, `mode`, etc.) are set on the `Datepicker` root component, not on `Datepicker.Field`.

### `Datepicker.CalendarIcon`

```tsx
<Datepicker.CalendarIcon
  iconName?: string             // Default: 'calendar'
  size?: number                  // Default: 20
  color?: string                 // Optional color override
  testID?: string
  accessibilityLabel?: string   // Default: 'Open date picker'
/>
```

**Note:** The calendar icon is automatically rendered if not provided. It opens the native date picker when pressed. Only used with `inputField` variant.

### `Datepicker.CompactFieldDisplay`

```tsx
<Datepicker.CompactFieldDisplay
  showIcon?: boolean            // Show calendar icon (default: true)
  iconName?: string             // Icon name (default: 'calendar')
  testID?: string               // Default: 'datepicker-compact-field-display'
  accessibilityLabel?: string   // Default: 'Date picker, current value {value}'
/>
```

**Note:** Only used with `compactField` variant. The `CompactFieldDisplay` is automatically rendered if not provided. When no date is selected, displays the format string as a hint.

### Types

| Type                  | Values                               |
| --------------------- | ------------------------------------ |
| `DatepickerVariant`   | `'inputField'` \| `'compactField'`   |
| `DatepickerMode`      | `'date'`                             |
| `DatepickerValueType` | `'date'` \| `'iso'` \| `'formatted'` |

## Usage Patterns

### Variants Overview

The datepicker supports two display variants:

| Variant        | Description                          | Use Cases                                        |
| -------------- | ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------ |
| `inputField`   | Form-style input with floating label | Forms, detailed data entry, validation-heavy UIs |
| `compactField` | Dropdown-style button                | Filters, compact layouts, inline date selection  |

### InputField Variant (default)

#### Basic datepicker (uncontrolled)

```tsx
<Datepicker defaultValue={null}>
  <Datepicker.Label>Date</Datepicker.Label>
  <Datepicker.Field placeholder="Select date" />
</Datepicker>
```

#### Controlled datepicker

```tsx
const [date, setDate] = useState<Date | null>(null);

<Datepicker value={date} onChange={setDate}>
  <Datepicker.Label>Date</Datepicker.Label>
  <Datepicker.Field placeholder="Select date" />
</Datepicker>;
```

#### With error state

```tsx
<Datepicker defaultValue={null} error="Please select a valid date">
  <Datepicker.Label>Date</Datepicker.Label>
  <Datepicker.Field />
</Datepicker>
```

**Note:** Helper text is automatically rendered when `error` exists - no need to include it in JSX.

#### With date constraints

```tsx
const today = new Date();
const maxDate = new Date(today.getFullYear() + 1, today.getMonth(), today.getDate());

<Datepicker defaultValue={null} minDate={today} maxDate={maxDate}>
  <Datepicker.Label>Date</Datepicker.Label>
  <Datepicker.Field placeholder="Select date" />
</Datepicker>;
```

#### Custom format

```tsx
<Datepicker defaultValue={null} format="MMM dd, yyyy">
  <Datepicker.Label>Date</Datepicker.Label>
  <Datepicker.Field />
</Datepicker>
```

#### With locale

```tsx
import { enUS, es, fr } from 'date-fns/locale';

<Datepicker defaultValue={null} locale={es} format="dd 'de' MMMM yyyy">
  <Datepicker.Label>Fecha</Datepicker.Label>
  <Datepicker.Field />
</Datepicker>;
```

#### Value type conversion

```tsx
// Return ISO string
<Datepicker
  defaultValue={null}
  valueType="iso"
  onChange={(isoString) => {
    console.log(isoString); // "2026-01-27T00:00:00.000Z"
  }}
>
  <Datepicker.Label>Date</Datepicker.Label>
  <Datepicker.Field />
</Datepicker>

// Return formatted string
<Datepicker
  defaultValue={null}
  valueType="formatted"
  format="yyyy-MM-dd"
  onChange={(formatted) => {
    console.log(formatted); // "2026-01-27"
  }}
>
  <Datepicker.Label>Date</Datepicker.Label>
  <Datepicker.Field />
</Datepicker>
```

#### Disabled and readonly states

```tsx
// Disabled
<Datepicker disabled defaultValue={new Date()}>
  <Datepicker.Label>Date</Datepicker.Label>
  <Datepicker.Field />
</Datepicker>

// Readonly
<Datepicker readonly defaultValue={new Date()}>
  <Datepicker.Label>Date (Read only)</Datepicker.Label>
  <Datepicker.Field />
</Datepicker>
```

### CompactField Variant

#### Basic compact datepicker

```tsx
<Datepicker variant="compactField" defaultValue={null} />
```

When no date is selected, the format string (e.g., "dd MMM yyyy") is shown as a hint.

#### Controlled compact datepicker

```tsx
const [date, setDate] = useState<Date | null>(null);

<Datepicker variant="compactField" value={date} onChange={setDate} />;
```

#### With customization (composition)

```tsx
// Without icon
<Datepicker variant="compactField" value={date} onChange={setDate}>
  <Datepicker.CompactFieldDisplay showIcon={false} />
</Datepicker>

// Custom icon
<Datepicker variant="compactField" value={date} onChange={setDate}>
  <Datepicker.CompactFieldDisplay iconName="notification" />
</Datepicker>
```

#### Compact with error state

```tsx
<Datepicker variant="compactField" defaultValue={null} error="Please select a date" />
```

#### Compact disabled and readonly

```tsx
// Disabled
<Datepicker variant="compactField" disabled defaultValue={new Date()} />

// Readonly
<Datepicker variant="compactField" readonly defaultValue={new Date()} />
```

## Context Architecture

The datepicker uses a **split context pattern** for optimal re-render performance. State is divided into 3 contexts based on update frequency:

| Context                   | Contains                                                                          | Updates when...                         | Hook                         |
| ------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- |
| `DatepickerConfigContext` | `mode`, `format`, `locale`, `minDate`, `maxDate`, `disabled`, `readonly`, `error` | Props change (rare)                     | `useDatepickerConfig()`      |
| `DatepickerStateContext`  | `isFocused`, `isPickerOpen`, `hasValue`, handlers, animations                     | Focus, picker open/close, empty↔filled | `useDatepickerInteraction()` |
| `DatepickerValueContext`  | `selectedDate`, `formattedValue`, `setDate`                                       | Every date selection (hot path)         | `useDatepickerValue()`       |

**Which hook each component uses:**

| Component               | Hooks Used                                                              | Re-renders on date selection? |
| ----------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------- |
| `CalendarIcon`          | `useDatepickerConfig`                                                   | No                            |
| `FloatingLabel`         | `useDatepickerInteraction`                                              | No (only on empty↔filled)    |
| `InputFieldDisplay`     | `useDatepickerConfig`, `useDatepickerInteraction`, `useDatepickerValue` | Yes (needs formatted value)   |
| `InputFieldContainer`   | `useDatepickerConfig`, `useDatepickerInteraction`                       | No                            |
| `CompactFieldContainer` | `useDatepickerInteraction`                                              | No                            |
| `CompactFieldDisplay`   | `useDatepickerConfig`, `useDatepickerInteraction`, `useDatepickerValue` | Yes (needs formatted value)   |
| `HelperText`            | `useDatepickerConfig`                                                   | No                            |

